# Lab git sync

Do not write or `scp` files onto the lab server (`kevin-mcdonald-ubu-01`, `kmactools`, or any other clone) when those files belong in git.

Workflow:

1. Edit and add files in the MacBook clone of the repo.
2. Commit (when the user asks, or when they asked to commit and push as part of this task).
3. `git push` to origin.
4. On the lab host only: `git pull` (or `git fetch` + checkout). Never copy the same tree over SSH.

If a lab clone already has leftover scp copies, delete those untracked files, then pull so git owns the tree.

Live systemd units under `/etc/systemd/system/` are installed from the pulled tree (`scripts/systemd/install-lab-loadgen-units.sh`). Do not treat `/etc` as the source of truth for script content.
